Mix components thoroughly and distribute the medium into culture vessels (e.g., 20 ml medium in 100 ml serum bottles or 5.0 ml medium in Hungate tubes) under a stream of N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (80:20, v/v), seal with butyl rubber stoppers and autoclave.  Allow to stand the autoclaved medium overnight. Add per liter the following solution from a sterile anaerobic stock (filter-sterilized and stored under a N<sub>2</sub> atmosphere):  <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 1 M Trimethylamine solution                            </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;10.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Prior to inoculation, add per liter the following solutions aseptically and anaerobically (autoclaved and stored under a N<sub>2</sub> atmosphere):  <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 5% L-Cysteine&#183;HCl&#183;H<sub>2</sub>O solution         </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;2.5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 5% Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O solution                      </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;2.5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
